<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Finding the area of a triangular land using Heron’s Formula</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>
A triangular piece of land has sides measuring <b>{@a@} m</b>, <b>{@b@} m</b>, and <b>{@c@} m</b>. Find the area of the land using Heron’s formula.
</p>

<p>
Give your answer correct to <b>2 decimal places</b>.
</p>

<p>
Area = [[input:ans1]] <b>\(\text{m}^2\)</b> [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]
</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>

<p>
The sides of the land are \(a = {@a@}\) m, \(b = {@b@}\) m and \(c = {@c@}\) m.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 1: Find the semi-perimeter (\(s\)).</strong>
</p>

<p>
\[
s = \frac{a+b+c}{2}
\]
</p>

<p>
\[
s = \frac{{@a@}+{@b@}+{@c@}}{2}
\]
</p>

<p>
\[
s = {@s@}
\]
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 2: Write Heron’s formula.</strong>
</p>

<p>
\[
A=\sqrt{s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c)}
\]
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 3: Substitute the values.</strong>
</p>

<p>
\[
A=\sqrt{{@s@}({@s@}-{@a@})({@s@}-{@b@})({@s@}-{@c@})}
\]
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 4: Simplify the brackets.</strong>
</p>

<p>
\[
A=\sqrt{{@s@}\times {@s-a@}\times {@s-b@}\times {@s-c@}}
\]
</p>

<p>
<strong>Step 5: Evaluate the square root.</strong>
</p>

<p>
\[
A \approx {@A_disp@}\text{ m}^2
\]
</p>

<p>
Therefore, the area of the land is:
</p>

<p>
\[
\boxed{{@A_disp@}\text{ m}^2}
\]
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
